  "query_preview": "..\nThe GFS ensemble suggests zonal flow and a weak ridge will be in\nplace through Thursday. There is some certainty of a trough moving\nin on Friday and precipitation, but there is not much certainty on\nhow much precipitation will fall. A Lake Wind Advisory has been \nissued for tomorrow for gusty southeast winds.\n\nBy Thursday, an upper-level low off the coast of central\nCalifornia will meander eastward over the Great Basin, enabling\nthe associated upper-level trough to begin digging over Montana. \nThe combination of trough-driven frontogenesis and moisture \nadvection will produce chances for precipitation beginning overnight\nThursday.\n\nAs of the most recent NBM run, precipitation is anticipated to \nend by Saturday morning. However, model agreement deteriorates \nsubstantially beyond this point. Forecast confidence is uncertain \nthrough the end of the week.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nThe only deviation was to winds for the lake wind advisory period.\n\nThere is moderate to high confidence in temperatures through\nThursday, and similar confidence for winds through tomorrow\nafternoon. There is low confidence in the trough timing late this\nweek and how much precipitation will fall.",
